# 换行规则。**它存在的理由是平台仓库里一次真实的失效**,不是补全强迫症。
#
# Actions 会把每个 `run:` 块原样写成临时文件交给 bash,带 CRLF 提交的工作流会在 runner 上报
# `syntax error near unexpected token $'do'`,而它指着的那一行完全没有问题。
# 平台仓库里那条保护写在了 `IM.Server/.gitattributes` 里——gitattributes 的模式相对于**它自己
# 所在的目录**,所以它管的是一个不存在的目录,从写下的那天起就匹配不到任何文件,
# 而它读起来像是生效的。这个仓库拆出来时把工作流和 gradlew 一并带走了,规则必须跟过来。
#
# Actions writes every `run:` block to a temp file verbatim, so a workflow committed with CRLF dies
# on the runner with `syntax error near unexpected token $'do'` pointing at a line that is fine.
# The equivalent rule in the platform repository sat one directory too deep and matched nothing for
# as long as it existed; this repository took the workflows and gradlew with it, so it takes the
# rule too.
#
# 刻意**不写** `* text=auto`:那会重写整棵树,代价远大于它买到的保证。
# 只钉 CI 与构建真正会执行的那几类文件。
# Deliberately no `* text=auto` — only the files CI and the builds actually execute.

.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.ps1     text eol=lf
*.psm1    text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
gradlew   text eol=lf

# 许可证副本。每个包目录随包发出去一份,`SdkPublishedMetadataTests` 要求它们与根上那份**逐字节**相同。
# 带 CRLF 提交的一份在 Windows 检出里(core.autocrlf=true)与 LF 的那份在磁盘上一模一样,
# 到了 Linux 上就不一样——2026-10-09 swift/LICENSE 就是这样骗过了本机 CI,在 GitHub 上
# 把单测套件弄红的。钉成 LF,两个平台上的字节才是同一份。
#
# Licence copies. Each package directory ships its own, and `SdkPublishedMetadataTests` wants every
# one byte-identical to the root copy. A copy committed with CRLF is identical to the LF one on a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) and different on Linux — which is how swift/LICENSE passed
# local CI and failed GitHub's unit suite on 2026-10-09. Pinned to LF, the bytes match everywhere.
LICENSE     text eol=lf
LICENSE.md  text eol=lf
